  "note": "What a quest needs in the world besides its dialogue: props anyone can click, actors each player owns, zones, per-player effects and named functions. tools/scenes_pack.py generates cobblers_scenes from this; positions come from the tool that builds the place (built_by), and tests check each marker is standable and each prop sits on something that tool builds (on).",
  "fields": {
    "area": "players inside run the scene's beat once a second; their actors exist only while they are inside",
    "markers": "named positions: [x, y, z] (feet), yaw, and slots (offsets for several players' copies side by side)",
    "actors": "Pokemon each player owns: species, level, conversation (opened on click by the owner), place rules (first whose condition holds)",
    "props": "shared interaction boxes (at, size) opening the clicker's own conversation; on = the block the prop sits on",
    "zones": "boxes that run named quest transitions for a player inside; no items",
    "effects": "per-player particles, sequences and push-backs while their condition holds",
    "npcs": "Cobblemon NPCs placed over RCON (classes load at server start)",
    "functions": "named command lists a dialogue runs as the player (effect scene_function)"
  },
